    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "in real digital photography, camera sensors can fail, resulting in 'dead/hot pixels' (corrupted white or black dots) or scratch marks. Using pure mathematical operations without any ready-made libraries, we will:\n",
        "\n",
        "Dynamically damage our image by injecting physical cracks/dust lines.\n",
        "Programmatically detect and map the damage using intensity threshold slicing.\n",
        "Implement a vectorized neighborhood healing algorithm (Inpainting) that automatically heals the damaged regions by smoothly blending neighbors together using localized spatial logic. In satellite imaging,medical scans, or digital photography, camera sensors often fail or get physically scratched this results in 'dead pixels' (black dots where no light was captured) or bright scratches. Standard photo editors usually blur the whole area to hide this, but blurring ruins the overall sharp quality and detail of the healthy parts of the image.\"\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DxOLKA4RzspW"
      }
